From 10e82319727986c52928db933622facb39761cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:33:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] io_uring: add vectored DMA-BUF block I/O

Extend ITER_DMABUF_MAP with a vector form so fixed READV and WRITEV
requests can describe multiple ranges within one registered dma-buf.
Import and validate the ranges in io_uring, retain one map reference
per request, and release the request-owned range storage with the
existing async read/write lifecycle.

Teach the block direct-I/O path to build one bio per range and
continue submitting bios until all ranges are consumed. Keep
queue-limit splitting and the NVMe PRP, SGL, and multipath paths
unchanged, and leave NVMe passthrough vectored dma-buf imports
disabled to preserve pinned-path routing.

Signed-off-by: Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>
